  ("Empirical and correlational evidence cited by Zajonc (1968)" 0.53208 0.93154 0.4038 0.42009 0.42009 0.01629 0.00437 0.3052 0.0656 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("in support of this hypothesis delineated what became the proto" 0.51625 0.93151 0.41799 0.43428 0.43428 0.01629 0.00437 0.3415 0.0127 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("typic methodologies used by other researchers to investigate the" 0.51625 0.93175 0.43218 0.44847 0.44847 0.01629 0.00437 0.3027 0.0335 "Times-Roman" 0.0127 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("exposure-affect relationship. The basic design of most labora-" 0.51667 0.93193 0.44606 0.46235 0.46235 0.01629 0.00437 0.2576 0.1019 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("tory mere exposure research is derived from Zajonc's (1968)" 0.51625 0.93152 0.46025 0.47654 0.47654 0.01629 0.00437 0.2554 0.0272 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Experiments 1-3, and the general approach used by later re-" 0.51667 0.93193 0.47444 0.49073 0.49073 0.01629 0.00437 0.2399 0.0844 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("searchers to examine the exposure-affect relationship in vivo" 0.51667 0.93178 0.48863 0.50492 0.50492 0.01629 0.00437 0.2451 0.0594 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("(i.e., in \"naturalistic\" studies of exposure and affect) is derived" 0.51625 0.93119 0.50282 0.51911 0.51911 0.01629 0.00434 0.2742 0.0282 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("from the correlational evidence cited by Zajonc. Thus, the typi-" 0.51667 0.93152 0.51701 0.5333 0.5333 0.01629 0.00437 0.3183 0.0307 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("cal laboratory study of exposure and affect involves presenting" 0.51667 0.93199 0.5312 0.54749 0.54749 0.01629 0.00437 0.2528 0.0191 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("varying numbers of exposures of neutral visual stimuli (e.g.," 0.51708 0.93128 0.54509 0.56137 0.56137 0.01629 0.00437 0.2775 0.0499 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("line drawings, nonsense words), after which some dependent" 0.51667 0.93121 0.55958 0.57587 0.57587 0.01629 0.00437 0.2678 0.0251 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("measure of affect regarding each stimulus is collected. Natural-" 0.51708 0.93193 0.57347 0.58976 0.58976 0.01629 0.00437 0.3307 0.0546 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("istic studies, which focus on stimuli present in the natural envi-" 0.51667 0.93151 0.58766 0.60395 0.60395 0.01629 0.00437 0.3366 0.0268 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ronment (e.g., names of public figures, common items), obtain" 0.51667 0.93133 0.60185 0.61814 0.61814 0.01629 0.00437 0.3827 0.0570 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("subjects' affect ratings of these stimuli using procedures similar" 0.51708 0.93197 0.61604 0.63233 0.63233 0.01629 0.00437 0.3288 0.0553 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("to those used in laboratory mere exposure studies but with fre-" 0.51667 0.93235 0.63023 0.64652 0.64652 0.01629 0.00437 0.3086 0.0132 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("quency of exposure estimated via some unobtrusive index such" 0.51667 0.93094 0.64442 0.66071 0.66071 0.01629 0.00437 0.3074 0.0476 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("as the Thorndike and Lorge (1944) word frequency count or" 0.51667 0.93156 0.65861 0.6749 0.6749 0.01629 0.00432 0.2120 0.0140 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("subjects' self-reports. Both laboratory and naturalistic studies" 0.51708 0.93228 0.6728 0.68909 0.68909 0.01629 0.00437 0.2597 0.0556 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("of the exposure effect generally utilize within-subjects designs," 0.51708 0.9317 0.68699 0.70328 0.70328 0.01629 0.00437 0.2721 0.0134 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("with each subject providing ratings of a number of stimuli that" 0.51667 0.93121 0.70118 0.71747 0.71747 0.01629 0.00437 0.3483 0.0297 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("differ in amount of previous exposure or familiarity." 0.51708 0.8604 0.71537 0.73166 0.73166 0.01629 0.00437 0.3488 0.0330 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Zajonc's (1968) initial correlational evidence indicated that" 0.5325 0.93121 0.73018 0.74646 0.74646 0.01629 0.00437 0.2559 0.0551 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("relationships exist between the Thorndike and Lorge (1944)" 0.51708 0.93194 0.74437 0.76065 0.76065 0.01629 0.00437 0.2304 0.0839 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("word frequency count and the evaluative meaning of a word, as" 0.51667 0.93143 0.75856 0.77485 0.77485 0.01629 0.00431 0.3399 0.0333 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("well as between word frequency and attitudes toward the object" 0.51667 0.93121 0.77275 0.78904 0.78904 0.01629 0.00437 0.3343 0.0266 "Times-Roman" 0.0122 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("described by a word. Presumably, these relationships reflect at-" 0.51667 0.93193 0.78694 0.80323 0.80323 0.01629 0.00437 0.3029 0.0613 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("titude enhancement resulting from repeated exposure to partic-" 0.51625 0.93197 0.80113 0.81742 0.81742 0.01629 0.00437 0.3109 0.0381 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ular words. Because these data are correlational, though, it is" 0.51708 0.93228 0.81532 0.83161 0.83161 0.01629 0.00437 0.2598 0.0261 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("impossible to demonstrate any causal relationship between" 0.51708 0.93133 0.8292 0.84549 0.84549 0.01629 0.00437 0.2824 0.0707 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("word frequency and evaluative meaning or attitude change." 0.51667 0.93165 0.84339 0.85968 0.85968 0.01629 0.00437 0.2334 0.0333 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("However, Zajonc also presented a series of experiments testing" 0.51708 0.93157 0.85789 0.87418 0.87418 0.01629 0.00437 0.3013 0.0596 "Times-Roman" 0.0122 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("his mere exposure hypothesis. Stronger evidence for the expo-" 0.51708 0.93236 0.87208 0.88837 0.88837 0.01629 0.00437 0.2521 0.0189 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("sure-affect relationship comes from these studies." 0.51667 0.84332 0.88627 0.90256 0.90256 0.01629 0.00437 0.3066 0.0698 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
