  ("In Zajonc's (1968) first experiment, subjects were presented" 0.08292 0.48119 0.08452 0.10081 0.10081 0.01629 0.00437 0.3046 0.0137 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("with a series of nonsense words at frequencies ranging from 0" 0.0675 0.48188 0.09871 0.115 0.115 0.01629 0.00437 0.2896 0.0297 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("to 25 exposures; they then rated each stimulus word for \"good-" 0.06792 0.48239 0.11259 0.12888 0.12888 0.01629 0.00437 0.3226 0.0130 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ness of meaning\" (i.e., the extent to which the word connotes" 0.06833 0.48227 0.12678 0.14307 0.14307 0.01629 0.00442 0.3144 0.0277 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("\"good\" vs. \"bad\" affect) on a seven-point scale. Zajonc found" 0.06792 0.4812 0.14066 0.15695 0.15695 0.01629 0.00437 0.2444 0.0500 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("a positive relationship between number of exposures and the" 0.0675 0.48195 0.15455 0.17083 0.17083 0.01629 0.00437 0.2649 0.0078 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("average goodness rating for a word. He then replicated this" 0.0675 0.48228 0.16874 0.18503 0.18503 0.01629 0.00437 0.2442 0.0488 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("study using a similar procedure but different stimuli: Chinese" 0.0675 0.48175 0.18293 0.19922 0.19922 0.01629 0.00437 0.3040 0.0359 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ideographs were substituted for the nonsense words used in Ex-" 0.06792 0.48192 0.19712 0.21341 0.21341 0.01629 0.00437 0.3119 0.0716 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("periment 1. The results of Experiment 2 were consistent with" 0.0675 0.48093 0.211 0.22729 0.22729 0.01629 0.00437 0.3319 0.0601 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("the findings of Zajonc's first study; again, rated goodness of" 0.0675 0.48196 0.22519 0.24148 0.24148 0.01629 0.00437 0.2330 0.0203 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("meaning was positively related to frequency of exposure." 0.0675 0.43832 0.23907 0.25536 0.25536 0.01629 0.00432 0.3196 0.0574 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Zajonc's (1968) third experiment investigated the extent to" 0.08292 0.48182 0.25326 0.26955 0.26955 0.01629 0.00437 0.2770 0.0551 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("which typical exposure effects could be obtained with socially" 0.06708 0.48135 0.26714 0.28343 0.28343 0.01629 0.00437 0.2837 0.0401 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("relevant stimuli. In this experiment, subjects were shown a se-" 0.0675 0.4815 0.28133 0.29762 0.29762 0.01629 0.00437 0.3481 0.0525 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
