  ("studies produces conflicting results, whereas meta-analysis of" 0.07042 0.4857 0.22457 0.24086 0.24086 0.01629 0.00441 0.2759 0.0456 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("all studies classified into salient dimensions for the variable in" 0.07042 0.4855 0.23876 0.25505 0.25505 0.01629 0.00441 0.2939 0.0165 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("question produces clearer and more consistent findings (see" 0.07042 0.48634 0.25295 0.26924 0.26924 0.01629 0.00441 0.2304 0.0552 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Light & Pillemer [1984], Rosenthal [1984], and Masters, Can-" 0.07125 0.4861 0.26653 0.28281 0.28281 0.01629 0.00441 0.3571 0.0354 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("tor, & Hedges [1988] for discussions of the value of meta-ana-" 0.07042 0.4861 0.28072 0.297 0.297 0.01629 0.00434 0.3167 0.0221 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  (#("lytic techniques in such circumstances). Finally, a fail-safe N" 62 63 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.07083 0.4859 0.29491 0.31119 0.31119 0.01629 0.00441 0.2723 0.0289 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("(Rosenthal, 1979, 1984) can be calculated for each effect size" 0.07042 0.48593 0.30879 0.32508 0.32508 0.01629 0.00423 0.2313 0.0763 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("estimate in the meta-analysis to assess the possible influence of" 0.07042 0.48571 0.32298 0.33927 0.33927 0.01629 0.0044 0.3126 0.0551 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("sampling bias (i.e., underestimate of unpublished, nonsignifi-" 0.07042 0.48606 0.33686 0.35315 0.35315 0.01629 0.00441 0.3026 0.0614 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("cant findings) on effect sizes (Criticism a)." 0.07042 0.3454 0.35105 0.36734 0.36734 0.01629 0.00436 0.3385 0.0280 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("The purpose of this article is to examine systematically the" 0.08542 0.48592 0.36493 0.38122 0.38122 0.01629 0.00441 0.3217 0.0265 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("influence of methodological and subject variables on the expo-" 0.07042 0.4861 0.37912 0.39541 0.39541 0.01629 0.0044 0.2693 0.0605 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("sure-affect relationship, in order to assess support for different" 0.07083 0.4858 0.393 0.40929 0.40929 0.01629 0.00441 0.2244 0.0698 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("theoretical models of the exposure effect. The analysis involves" 0.07042 0.48686 0.40719 0.42348 0.42348 0.01629 0.00441 0.3054 0.0692 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("several steps. First, studies of the exposure-affect relationship" 0.07083 0.48602 0.42108 0.43736 0.43736 0.01629 0.00441 0.2328 0.0445 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("that appeared in the first two decades following publication of" 0.07083 0.48572 0.43527 0.45155 0.45155 0.01629 0.00434 0.2783 0.0259 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Zajonc's (1968) monograph are reviewed. The influence of each" 0.07083 0.48916 0.44915 0.46544 0.46544 0.01629 0.0043 0.3288 0.0560 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("methodological and subject variable on the exposure effect is" 0.07083 0.48643 0.46334 0.47963 0.47963 0.01629 0.00429 0.2452 0.1003 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("assessed using meta-analytic techniques (Rosenthal, 1984). For" 0.07083 0.48572 0.47753 0.49382 0.49382 0.01629 0.00441 0.2992 0.0518 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("reasons that are discussed later, certain variables (e.g., stimulus" 0.07125 0.48645 0.49141 0.5077 0.5077 0.01629 0.00441 0.3026 0.0485 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("complexity) could not be subjected to meta-analysis. However," 0.07125 0.48624 0.50529 0.52158 0.52158 0.01629 0.0044 0.3120 0.0795 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("these variables are discussed in the following sections as they" 0.07083 0.48552 0.51917 0.53546 0.53546 0.01629 0.00433 0.2427 0.0337 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("apply to particular issues. The implications of this review and" 0.07083 0.48536 0.53336 0.54965 0.54965 0.01629 0.00439 0.3059 0.0367 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("analysis are discussed in the context of theoretical models of" 0.07125 0.48654 0.54755 0.56384 0.56384 0.01629 0.00438 0.2484 0.0523 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("mere exposure effects. Empirical support for these models is" 0.07125 0.48643 0.56174 0.57803 0.57803 0.01629 0.00441 0.2960 0.0334 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("assessed, and modifications in the best-supported model of ex-" 0.07125 0.48651 0.57563 0.59191 0.59191 0.01629 0.00435 0.3066 0.0580 "Times-Roman" 0.0129 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("posure effects are described, which allow the model to better" 0.07125 0.48614 0.58982 0.6061 0.6061 0.01629 0.00438 0.2861 0.0448 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("accommodate the range of findings in this area. An evolution-" 0.07083 0.48652 0.6037 0.61999 0.61999 0.01629 0.0044 0.3305 0.0912 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ary basis of the exposure effect is briefly discussed in the context" 0.07125 0.48579 0.61758 0.63387 0.63387 0.01629 0.00429 0.3003 0.0211 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("of findings from this review." 0.07167 0.25409 0.63177 0.64806 0.64806 0.01629 0.00419 0.3388 0.0135 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Meta-Analysis" 0.22583 0.33234 0.66527 0.68328 0.68328 0.018 nil 0.4141 0.1065 "Times-Roman" 0.0139 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  (#("Inclusion Criteria" 0 18 (pdf-text-emph italic)) 0.07167 0.20261 0.69195 0.70843 0.70843 0.01648 0.00445 0.2746 0.0680 "Times-Italic" 0.0135 nil t 0 "Times-Italic" nil)
  ("This review and meta-analysis of the exposure-affect rela-" 0.08708 0.48693 0.71599 0.73227 0.73227 0.01629 0.00434 0.2564 0.0300 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("tionship includes studies of unreinforced exposure and affect" 0.07125 0.48664 0.72987 0.74616 0.74616 0.01629 0.00428 0.2132 0.0546 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("that were published between 1968 and 1987. The review in-" 0.07125 0.4865 0.74406 0.76035 0.76035 0.01629 0.0043 0.2504 0.0262 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("cludes only articles published after Zajonc's (1968) monograph" 0.07167 0.48593 0.75794 0.77423 0.77423 0.01629 0.00441 0.3104 0.0419 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("for several reasons. First, studies in this area conducted prior to" 0.07167 0.48641 0.77213 0.78842 0.78842 0.01629 0.00441 0.2746 0.0172 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("the mid-1960s were often methodologically unsound (see Za-" 0.07167 0.48692 0.78632 0.80261 0.80261 0.01629 0.00441 0.2824 0.0201 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("jonc, 1968). Many early studies used improper control groups" 0.07 0.48686 0.8002 0.81649 0.81649 0.01629 0.00441 0.3125 0.0332 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("or conditions, or no controls at all, making it impossible to de-" 0.07167 0.48694 0.81439 0.83068 0.83068 0.01629 0.00447 0.3434 0.0142 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("rive effect size estimates for meta-analysis. With the publication" 0.07208 0.48633 0.82796 0.84425 0.84425 0.01629 0.00441 0.3952 0.0253 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("of Zajonc's seminal paper and his description of experimental" 0.07125 0.48618 0.84215 0.85844 0.85844 0.01629 0.00441 0.3010 0.0139 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("approaches to the study of exposure effects, the methodologies" 0.07167 0.48728 0.85635 0.87263 0.87263 0.01629 0.00438 0.2707 0.0741 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("used in these studies have improved markedly and have become" 0.07208 0.48634 0.86992 0.88621 0.88621 0.01629 0.00441 0.3485 0.0300 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("much more consistent across experiments. Limiting this review" 0.07167 0.48596 0.8838 0.90009 0.90009 0.01629 0.00441 0.3649 0.0372 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("to papers published since 1968 allows for discussion of individ-" 0.51625 0.93194 0.0839 0.10019 0.10019 0.01629 0.00441 0.2954 0.0130 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ual experiments; if the many pre-1968 studies were included, it" 0.51667 0.93205 0.09809 0.11438 0.11438 0.01629 0.00441 0.3461 0.0206 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("would simply become unwieldy owing to the large number of" 0.51667 0.93196 0.11197 0.12826 0.12826 0.01629 0.00441 0.3378 0.0404 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("papers that have little value concerning the theoretical and em-" 0.51708 0.93277 0.12617 0.14245 0.14245 0.01629 0.00441 0.3029 0.0429 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("pirical issues raised in this review. Stang (1974b) reviewed stud-" 0.51667 0.93193 0.14005 0.15634 0.15634 0.01629 0.00441 0.3322 0.0423 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ies in this area that were published prior to 1968." 0.51708 0.83871 0.15424 0.17053 0.17053 0.01629 0.00441 0.3296 0.0185 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("This review includes only experiments that investigate affect" 0.5325 0.93205 0.16812 0.18441 0.18441 0.01629 0.00441 0.3265 0.0300 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("changes in response to mere (i.e., unreinforced) exposure to vi-" 0.51667 0.93235 0.18231 0.1986 0.1986 0.01629 0.00441 0.3177 0.0523 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("sual and auditory stimuli. The vast majority of mere exposure" 0.51708 0.93259 0.19619 0.21248 0.21248 0.01629 0.00441 0.3318 0.0264 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("experiments have studied attitudes toward these stimuli. Stud-" 0.51708 0.93235 0.21038 0.22667 0.22667 0.01629 0.00441 0.3274 0.0811 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ies that involve exposure to other types of stimuli (i.e., olfactory" 0.51708 0.93218 0.22457 0.24086 0.24086 0.01629 0.00441 0.3620 0.0184 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("and gustatory) present a different set of methodological issues" 0.51708 0.9327 0.23845 0.25474 0.25474 0.01629 0.00441 0.2562 0.0240 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("that are only tangentially related to findings obtained using bet-" 0.51708 0.93277 0.25264 0.26893 0.26893 0.01629 0.00441 0.3238 0.0262 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ter-controlled visual and auditory stimuli. Certain key variables" 0.51708 0.9327 0.26653 0.28281 0.28281 0.01629 0.00441 0.3375 0.0891 "Times-Roman" 0.0127 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("(e.g., exposure duration, stimulus complexity) are difficult to" 0.51708 0.93225 0.28041 0.2967 0.2967 0.01629 0.00441 0.3135 0.0315 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("measure in olfactory and gustatory stimuli, making interexperi-" 0.5175 0.93279 0.2946 0.31089 0.31089 0.01629 0.00441 0.3826 0.0558 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ment comparisons difficult. In addition, exposure to certain" 0.5175 0.93134 0.30879 0.32508 0.32508 0.01629 0.00441 0.2862 0.0337 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("gustatory and olfactory stimuli may be reinforcing in and of" 0.51667 0.93158 0.32267 0.33896 0.33896 0.01629 0.0043 0.2805 0.0619 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("itself (see, e.g., C. S. Crandall's, 1984, study of exposure effects" 0.51708 0.93262 0.33686 0.35315 0.35315 0.01629 0.00441 0.3294 0.0316 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("with doughnuts), so that such experiments can no longer be" 0.51708 0.93217 0.35074 0.36703 0.36703 0.01629 0.00441 0.2521 0.0293 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("strictly classified as mere exposure research. Although these" 0.51708 0.93217 0.36493 0.38122 0.38122 0.01629 0.00441 0.2672 0.0451 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("studies are not included in the meta-analysis, they will be dis-" 0.51708 0.9328 0.37881 0.3951 0.3951 0.01629 0.00441 0.3091 0.0449 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("cussed in later sections of this article." 0.51708 0.7613 0.393 0.40929 0.40929 0.01629 0.00441 0.2784 0.0424 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Studies that include any type of reinforcement introduced" 0.53292 0.93244 0.40719 0.42348 0.42348 0.01629 0.00441 0.2520 0.0481 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("during the exposure or rating phases of the experiment are not" 0.51708 0.93204 0.42108 0.43736 0.43736 0.01629 0.00442 0.2958 0.0449 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("included in the meta-analysis, to avoid contaminating the anal-" 0.5175 0.93277 0.43527 0.45155 0.45155 0.01629 0.00442 0.3356 0.0570 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ysis with experiments investigating phenomena other than un-" 0.5175 0.93276 0.44915 0.46544 0.46544 0.01629 0.00441 0.3247 0.0243 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("reinforced stimulus exposure. A number of experiments inves-" 0.51708 0.93234 0.46334 0.47963 0.47963 0.01629 0.00441 0.3421 0.0675 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("tigating familiarity effects in social settings (e.g., Ebbeson, Kjos," 0.51708 0.9325 0.47753 0.49382 0.49382 0.01629 0.00441 0.3393 0.0503 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("& Konecni, 1976; Segal, 1974) were eliminated on the basis of" 0.5175 0.93302 0.49141 0.5077 0.5077 0.01629 0.00441 0.3426 0.0132 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("this criterion, because it was not clear to what extent attitude" 0.5175 0.93259 0.50529 0.52158 0.52158 0.01629 0.00441 0.2972 0.0248 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("changes in these studies were induced by mere exposure or by" 0.51708 0.93218 0.51948 0.53577 0.53577 0.01629 0.00441 0.2745 0.0523 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("reinforcement derived from repeated social interaction." 0.5175 0.88292 0.53336 0.54965 0.54965 0.01629 0.00441 0.2859 0.0930 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("In addition, the numerous studies of the relationship between" 0.53333 0.93217 0.54724 0.56353 0.56353 0.01629 0.00441 0.3482 0.0135 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("novelty-familiarity and infant attention/looking time that fol-" 0.5175 0.93276 0.56144 0.57772 0.57772 0.01629 0.00441 0.3129 0.1260 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("lowed Fantz's (1964) experiment (e.g., Balogh & Porter, 1986;" 0.5175 0.93277 0.57532 0.59161 0.59161 0.01629 0.00441 0.3287 0.0379 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Faw & Nunnally, 1968; D. Greenberg, Uzgiris, & Hunt, 1970;" 0.51792 0.93319 0.58982 0.6061 0.6061 0.01629 0.00441 0.3740 0.0266 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Hunter, Ames, & Koopman, 1983; Hunter, Ross, & Ames," 0.5175 0.93213 0.60339 0.61968 0.61968 0.01629 0.00441 0.3409 0.0504 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("1982; Nachmann, Stern, & Best, 1986) are not included in the" 0.51958 0.93258 0.61758 0.63387 0.63387 0.01629 0.00437 0.3385 0.0361 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("meta-analysis. The relationship between attention and affect" 0.51792 0.93247 0.63177 0.64806 0.64806 0.01629 0.00441 0.2792 0.0920 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("may vary as a function of experimental paradigm and age of" 0.51792 0.93241 0.64565 0.66194 0.66194 0.01629 0.00429 0.2762 0.0274 "Times-Roman" 0.0122 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("subject (see D. Greenberg et al., 1970; Nachmann et al., 1986;" 0.5175 0.93317 0.65984 0.67613 0.67613 0.01629 0.00443 0.3263 0.0459 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Wetherford & Cohen, 1973), and research suggests that both" 0.51792 0.9326 0.67403 0.69032 0.69032 0.01629 0.00441 0.2967 0.0738 "Times-Roman" 0.0123 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("pleasant stimuli and extremely unpleasant stimuli (e.g., depic-" 0.51792 0.93321 0.68791 0.7042 0.7042 0.01629 0.00441 0.3448 0.0539 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("tions of violent acts) are associated with increased attention and" 0.5175 0.93202 0.7021 0.71839 0.71839 0.01629 0.00441 0.3223 0.0322 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("scrutiny (Scrivner & Safer, 1988). Thus, treating visual prefer-" 0.51792 0.93273 0.71599 0.73227 0.73227 0.01629 0.00441 0.2880 0.0542 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("ence or fixation time as an affect measure comparable to those" 0.51792 0.93301 0.73018 0.74646 0.74646 0.01629 0.00438 0.3240 0.0301 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("obtained via verbal report is unwarranted. Studies of novelty-" 0.51792 0.93235 0.74406 0.76035 0.76035 0.01629 0.00441 0.2777 0.0564 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("familiarity and infant attention are discussed later, in the con-" 0.51792 0.93277 0.75825 0.77454 0.77454 0.01629 0.00434 0.2746 0.0694 "Times-Roman" 0.0122 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("text of findings from exposure effects research." 0.51792 0.82458 0.77213 0.78842 0.78842 0.01629 0.0042 0.2791 0.0250 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Finally, the meta-analysis includes only studies that used hu-" 0.53375 0.93319 0.78632 0.80261 0.80261 0.01629 0.00441 0.3074 0.0492 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("man subjects. A number of investigations in this area have used" 0.51792 0.93203 0.8002 0.81649 0.81649 0.01629 0.00441 0.3625 0.0284 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("infrahuman subjects (e.g., Navarick & Strouthes, 1969;" 0.51792 0.93319 0.81408 0.83037 0.83037 0.01629 0.00441 0.3477 0.0773 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("Strouthes, 1971); these experiments were reviewed by Hill" 0.51833 0.93285 0.82827 0.84456 0.84456 0.01629 0.00441 0.2843 0.0670 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("(1978), who found strong support for the existence of exposure" 0.5175 0.93301 0.84215 0.85844 0.85844 0.01629 0.00427 0.2820 0.0479 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("effects in infrahumans. However, the methodologies, stimuli," 0.51792 0.93254 0.85604 0.87233 0.87233 0.01629 0.00422 0.3217 0.0394 "Times-Roman" 0.0124 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("and dependent measures used in these studies differ so signifi-" 0.51792 0.93354 0.87023 0.88652 0.88652 0.01629 0.00441 0.2594 0.0239 "Times-Roman" 0.0125 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
  ("cantly from those used in exposure effects research with human" 0.5175 0.93217 0.88411 0.9004 0.9004 0.01629 0.00441 0.3462 0.0405 "Times-Roman" 0.0126 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil))
  (4
  ("268" 0.07042 0.09774 0.05251 0.07222 0.07222 0.01971 nil 0.0000 0.0273 "Times-Roman" 0.0144 nil nil 0 "Times-Roman" nil)
